course: dictionary
lesson: 13898
title: Clergy and laity
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come in pairs that name two different groups of people. Context helps you see which group is which. «The vicar led the prayers, and the laity joined in the singing.» The vicar is a priest who leads the service. The laity are the rest of the people in the church.
explain: Read the clues: the vicar leads, and the others follow, sing and listen. So laity must mean the ordinary churchgoers who are not priests. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The ordinary churchgoers joined in the singing» still makes sense.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. «The science book was hard, so the writer explained it simply for the laity.» Here laity means people who are not experts in a subject. The clue is that the writer made it simple for them. Read the clues first, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: Look for the word lay as well. «Dad is a lay reader, so he reads at church, but he is not a priest.» Lay is an adjective: it describes a person. Laity is the noun for the whole group of ordinary members.
fact: Laity is a noun, and it is often used with «the»: the laity.
fact: «Laity» means the ordinary members of a church who are not priests, ministers or clergy.
fact: «Clergy» means the priests, vicars and ministers who lead church services.
fact: «The clergy and the laity» means all the people in a church: the leaders and the ordinary members.
fact: «Laity» can also mean people who are not experts in a subject.
exercise: «The vicar led the service, and the laity sang the hymns.» Who are the laity in this sentence? | The bishop alone | *The ordinary churchgoers who are not priests | The clergy who lead the service | The Bible
exercise: «The science book was full of hard words, so it was written simply for the laity.» What does laity mean here? | *People who are not experts in the subject | Scientists who wrote the book | Teachers who mark the work | People who lead church services
exercise: Which word means the ordinary churchgoers, not the priests? | vicar | *laity | clergy | minister
test: «Dad is a lay reader, so he reads at church, but he is not a priest.» What does lay tell you about Dad? | *He is not a priest or minister | He can sing better than the choir | He is a very old church member | He is always late for services
test: «The clergy and the laity sat together for the prayers.» Who are the laity in this sentence? | *The ordinary church members | The people who lead the prayers | The priests and ministers only | The people who built the church
exam: Which sentence uses laity to mean people who are not experts? | «Only the clergy can give the blessing.» | «The laity sang the final hymn.» | «The laity read Bible passages aloud.» | *«The article was hard to follow, so it was simplified for the laity.»
